@baseUrl = https://localhost:7217

# ConferenceProFlow — M2.5 end-to-end demonstration
# Run these requests from top to bottom, stopping AFTER demoCreateSession
# to run docs/ALLOCATION_E2E_SEED.sql in ConferenceProFlowAllocation.
# Start both the Registration API and Allocation Worker before registration requests.
# IMPORTANT: For a second run, create a NEW session and use NEW participant email addresses.
# STOP after demoCreateSession succeeds. Copy its response body `id` into @SessionIdText in
# docs/ALLOCATION_E2E_SEED.sql, then execute the SQL script against the Allocation database.
# The script creates capacity = 2 and ReservedCount = 0 for this session.
# Only after seeding, continue with requests 3 through 8.

### 1. Create a dedicated demo conference
# @name demoCreateConference
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/conferences
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "ConferenceProFlow Allocation Demo 2027",
  "startsAtUtc": "2027-06-01T08:00:00Z",
  "endsAtUtc": "2027-06-02T18:00:00Z"
}

### 2. Create a demo session (its ID is needed to seed Allocation inventory)
# @name demoCreateSession
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/conferences/{{demoCreateConference.response.body.$.id}}/sessions
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Concurrency-Safe Seat Allocation",
  "startsAtUtc": "2027-06-01T10:00:00Z",
  "endsAtUtc": "2027-06-01T11:30:00Z"
}

### 3. Create first demo participant
# @name demoCreateParticipant1
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/participants
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "displayName": "Nora Ellis",
  "email": "nora.ellis.demo2027a@example.com"
}

### 4. Register first participant for the demo session
# @name demoCreateRegistration1
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/registrations
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "participantId": "{{demoCreateParticipant1.response.body.$.id}}",
  "sessionId": "{{demoCreateSession.response.body.$.id}}"
}

### 5. Create second demo participant
# @name demoCreateParticipant2
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/participants
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "displayName": "Ethan Brooks",
  "email": "ethan.brooks.demo2027a@example.com"
}

### 6. Register second participant for the same session
# @name demoCreateRegistration2
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/registrations
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "participantId": "{{demoCreateParticipant2.response.body.$.id}}",
  "sessionId": "{{demoCreateSession.response.body.$.id}}"
}

### 7. Create third demo participant
# @name demoCreateParticipant3
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/participants
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "displayName": "Maya Chen",
  "email": "maya.chen.demo2027a@example.com"
}

### 8. Register third participant (capacity was only 2)
# @name demoCreateRegistration3
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/registrations
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "participantId": "{{demoCreateParticipant3.response.body.$.id}}",
  "sessionId": "{{demoCreateSession.response.body.$.id}}"
}

### 9. Inspect the original Registration-side status (still Pending in M2.5)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/registrations/{{demoCreateRegistration1.response.body.$.id}}

### 10. Inspect the other two Registration-side statuses
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/registrations/{{demoCreateRegistration2.response.body.$.id}}

### 11. Inspect the final Registration-side status
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/registrations/{{demoCreateRegistration3.response.body.$.id}}